.TH PATH_IS_ABSOLUTE_B 3
.SH NAME
path_is_absolute_b \- check if a path buffer contains an absolute path
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <path.h>
.PP
.BI "int path_is_absolute_b(const char* " x ", size_t " n ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B path_is_absolute_b
determines whether the path string provided in the buffer
.I x
of length
.I n
is an absolute path.
.PP
The definition of an absolute path is platform-dependent:
.TP
.B Windows
Uses the Windows API
.BR PathIsRelativeW
(via UTF-8 to UTF-16 conversion) to determine if the path is rooted.
.TP
.B POSIX
A path is considered absolute if it starts with the root directory separator ('/').
.TP
.B Windows/MinGW
Supports both standard POSIX root styles and drive-letter specifications (e.g., "C:\") if the platform is configured for Windows support.
.SH RETURN VALUE
.TP
.B 1
The path is absolute.
.TP
.B 0
The path is relative.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR path_is_absolute (3),
.BR path_is_root (3)